<!--
    Material Symbols "library_music", for the Select Library row.

    The path is upstream's verbatim. Material Symbols exports on a
    viewBox of "0 -960 960 960", so every y is negative, and
    VectorDrawable has no viewBox origin: only viewportWidth/Height
    measured from 0,0. The group's translateY of 960 supplies the
    missing offset.

    The other ic_browse_* icons instead carry coordinates rewritten into
    positive space. That is the same picture arrived at by editing every
    number in the path, which is worth avoiding when a transform does it
    exactly and leaves the glyph diffable against upstream.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportHeight="960"
    android:viewportWidth="960"
    android:width="24dp">

    <group android:translateY="960">
